    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-p/q3-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Fill in a diagram: (a) The intersection is 0.45 −0.25 = 0.20. The B-only region is 0.80 −0.45 = 0.35, [B1] and the exterior is 1 −0.80 = 0.20 . [A1] (b) Since P(B′) = 0.45 and P(A′) = 0.55, (i) P(A | B′) = 0.25/0.45 . [M1] [A1] = 5/9\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-p/q3-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(ii) P(B′ | A′) = 0.20/0.55 . [M1] [A1] = 4/11 (c) The condition A′ ∪B′ excludes only the intersection, and A ∩B′ lies entirely within the condition: [B1] [A1] By De Morgan’s law, the conditioning probability is 1 −P(A ∩B) = 1 −0.20. Its intersection with A ∩B′ remains A ∩B′. The result is 0.25/0.80 = 5/16 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 3 is 10 marks.</p>"
