    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-p/q7-question-1.svg\" alt=\"C B A A box of mass 76 kg is attached by a string to one end B of a uniform rod AB of length 5 m and mass 24 kg . The rod is held horizontally in equilibrium by two smooth cylindrical pegs, one at A and one at C , where AC = 2 m , as shown in the figure above.\" style=\"--madas-width:561.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-p/q7-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Calculate the magnitude of the forces exerted by each of the pegs onto the rod. ( ) 7\" style=\"--madas-width:574.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-p/q7-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Starting with a diagram noting that the rod is uniform: Let the upward reaction at C be RC and the downward reaction at A have magnitude RA. [B1] [A1] Moments about A give 2RC = 24g(2.5) + 76g(5) . [A1] = 440g\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-p/q7-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Then RC = 220g = 2156 N . [M1] [A1] The scan alternatively takes moments about C. The beam acts 0.5 m to its right and the diver acts 3 m to its right, giving 2RA = 24g(0.5) + 76g(3) . = 240g The force at A is downward: From vertical balance RA = RC −100g = 120g = 1176 N . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 7 is 7 marks.</p>"
