    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-p/q10",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-p/q10-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A particle is projected from a point O on level horizontal ground with speed of ms− at an angle ψ to the horizontal, where 1 15 23.8 tan ψ = . 8 The particle is moving freely under gravity, reaching a greatest height of H m above the ground before it lands on the ground at a point A . a) Determine the distance OA ( ) 6 b) Find the value of H . ( ) 3 c) Calculate, to three significant figures, the speed of the particle when it is at a height of 20 m above the ground. ( ) 6\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-p/q10-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:572.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-p/q10-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Starting with a diagram:\" style=\"--madas-width:550.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-p/q10-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"From the 8-15-17 triangle the horizontal and initial vertical velocities are 11.2 and 21 m s−1. (a) The positive root of 21t −4.9t2 = 0 [B1] [A1] is t = 30/7 s. [M1] [A1] Hence OA = 11.2(30/7) = 48 m . [M1] [A1] (b) The time to the highest point is half the flight time, 15/7 seconds: Using displacement instead gives H = 21(15/7) −4.9(15/7)2 . = 22.5 At the top 0 = 212 −2gH, [M1] giving H = 22.5 . [M1] [A1] (c) At height 20 m, the squared vertical speed is 212 −2g(20) = 49. [B1] [M1] [A1] At this height vy = ±7 m s−1; the two positions have the same speed. Alternatively conserve energy: v2 = 23.82 −2(9.8)(20) = 174.44, again giving 13.2 m s−1.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
