    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-p/q12-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) The displacement of A over five seconds is 15i −10j in metres: [B1] [A1] Its constant velocity is 3i −2j in m s−1, so its position is (3t −2)i + (3 −2t)j in metres: [M1] [M1] [A1] (b) At t = 30 the collision is at 88i −57j. [B1] [A1] Subtract the coordinates of B at 10 seconds from the common collision position: (88, −57) −(8, 3) = (80, −60). Divide each component by 30 −10 = 20. The displacement of B from t = 10 [A1] is 80i −60j over 20 seconds, so V = 4i −3j . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
